Key Type Content <code>path</code> <code>str</code>, or <code>pathlib.Path</code> with <code>as_path=True</code> Path of the file, starting with <code>root</code> <code>line_number</code> <code>int</code> 1-based line number <code>line_text</code> <code>str</code> The whole line, including its line ending <code>matches</code> <code>list[str]</code> In the current release, one item: the line with surrounding whitespace removed <p><code>matches</code> does not yet contain the individual regex matches. To find the matched substrings, run Python's <code>re</code> on <code>line_text</code>:</p> <pre><code>import re

rx = re.compile(r"TODO\s*(\w+)")
for hit in vexy_glob.search(r"TODO", "*.py"):
    for m in rx.finditer(hit["line_text"]):
        print(hit["path"], hit["line_number"], m.group(1))
</code></pre> <p>A line that matches several times still produces one result.</p> <p>Lines that are not valid UTF-8 are decoded with replacement characters (<code>U+FFFD</code>).</p>
